  "title": "Cancellation-test failure paths still signal cached, possibly recycled PIDs",
  "detail": "At test/failure-injection.test.ts:1133 and :1349 the new Set removes pids only after successful settlement and disappearance checks. If settlement rejects after the descendants have exited, the finally block sends SIGKILL to every retained numeric pid without confirming it is still the original process, which is the recycled-id hazard #441 describes. Executing the test body with an injected settlement failure and a fake signal backend recorded two SIGKILL attempts against simulated recycled ids. Make the failure paths ownership-aware too: only signal a pid whose identity (for example start time or the invocation marker) still matches what the test recorded, or drop pids once they are known gone regardless of how settlement ended."
 }
]
